From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 05:26:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: deinit spectral and CFR before freeing the
 pdev's DP

ath11k_dp_pdev_free() calls ath11k_debugfs_unregister(), which removes
the pdev's debugfs directory recursively, and with it the spectral and
CFR files and relay buffers inside it. ath11k_core_reconfigure_on_crash()
deinitialized spectral and CFR only after that, so their
debugfs_remove() and relay_close() ran on dentries that were already
removed and freed. Every firmware crash recovery of a radio with
spectral scan enabled could oops there:

  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 0000000000000098
  pc : down_write+0x70/0xa0
  lr : __simple_recursive_removal+0x5c/0x1fc
  Call trace:
   down_write+0x70/0xa0 (P)
   __simple_recursive_removal+0x5c/0x1fc
   simple_recursive_removal+0x14/0x20
   debugfs_remove+0x58/0x7c
   ath11k_spectral_deinit+0x9c/0x120 [ath11k]
   ath11k_core_restart+0x98/0x208 [ath11k]

Deinit them first, in the order ath11k_core_pdev_destroy() already
uses.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
index b7cac0b..c0c079e 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
@@ -2446,9 +2446,10 @@ static int ath11k_core_reconfigure_on_crash(struct ath11k_base *ab)
 		ath11k_hif_ce_irq_disable(ab);
 	}
 
-	ath11k_dp_pdev_free(ab);
+	/* Before ath11k_dp_pdev_free(), which removes the debugfs they live in */
 	ath11k_cfr_deinit(ab);
 	ath11k_spectral_deinit(ab);
+	ath11k_dp_pdev_free(ab);
 	ath11k_ce_cleanup_pipes(ab);
 	ath11k_wmi_detach(ab);
 	ath11k_dp_pdev_reo_cleanup(ab);
